    "body": "## Evidence\n\n15 Oct repository audit found **no staff list/read APIs** for operations and Business Workspace reference screens are fixtures only. This is NEW BACKEND query capability; existing [GLO-83](https://linear.app/ahme-hassan/issue/GLO-83/build-hub-operations-console)/223/125 are UI projects, which remain paused.\n\n## Implement ONLY NestJS owner-module API read contracts\n\n* Admin: operational order attention queue, pending decisions, sourcing failures, fulfillment exceptions (small paginated/filterable summaries).\n* Supplier: own consolidated PO inbox and line details with own confirmed/ready states; no PII or competitors' prices.\n* Hub: assigned location receivable PO lines, per-Order preparation queue, ready shipments, optional assigned dispatch runs.\n* Driver: own manifest/details including necessary secured pin/phone/COD and current status; reuse existing driver read API; no duplicate endpoint.\n* Cashier/Admin: unsettled expected/declared collections + discrepancies, settlement history scoped to authorized hub.\n* Support: case/exception actionable list if existing model permits; use canonical IDs, no independent state ownership.\n* Use typed DTOs, bounded pagination, whitelisted sorting/filters, role+resource ownership checks, stable consistent statuses, no new denormalized parallel source of truth unless measured necessary.\n\n## DoD\n\nAPI documentation and role-by-role HTTP/DB tests show each actor sees its own work only; Driver B/Supplier B/Hub B denied cross-tenant/foreign records, PII minimized. No Next.js, dashboard layouts, auth UI, live SSE or generic reporting engine.",
